Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:40:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/15] [B70][XPU][Attention] INT8 KV: head_size guard + B70
 check for Qwen hybrid shapes

- paged_decode.hpp: instantiate the INT8 per-token-head decode configs only
  for head sizes that are a multiple of 64 (the block-local split layout
  needs 64-byte aligned K/V surface bases: V starts head_size bytes into the
  slot). Other head sizes fall through to the unsupported-dtype check.
- tests/flash_attn/int8_kv_b70_check.py: standalone GPU check (no pytest)
  for head_size 256, bf16 Q, num_kv_heads 2/4, GQA 8/6, block sizes 64, 832
  and 4352 (padded pages), random lengths and block placement, garbage in
  unused slots and scales: native decode, uniform q_len 8 spec-decode verify,
  and prefill through a dequantized bf16 scratch, against an fp32 reference
  on the same quantized cache (rel err <= 0.03, cos >= 0.999); --bench times
  the decode kernel INT8 vs bf16 KV.

